From 62598e0f52a7a7f8422262a8db2c00ce20c49534 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:55:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v2/plugin: add subprocess plugin API for language extensions

Gazelle language extensions can now be written in any language. A
plugin is an executable that Gazelle starts as a subprocess and talks
to with JSON-RPC 2.0, one JSON message per line, over the plugin's
stdin and stdout. Plugins take part in a run exactly like extensions
compiled into a gazelle_binary: their directives are recognized, their
rules are generated, merged and indexed, and their dependencies are
resolved against the shared rule index.

* v2/plugin/protocol: the wire schema (Go structs with lowerCamelCase
  JSON names) and a small JSON-RPC connection. Methods mirror the v2
  extension interfaces: initialize (name, kinds, known directives,
  capabilities), configure, fix, generate, imports, resolve, find,
  onResolve, onFinish and shutdown. While handling resolve or find, a
  plugin can call back into Gazelle with index/find, which applies
  gazelle:resolve overrides, then the rule index, then finders.
* v2/plugin: Language adapts a plugin process to the v2 interfaces.
  Per-directory configuration is an opaque JSON value stored in
  Config.Exts, so plugins stay stateless. Errors carry severities;
  a crashed plugin is reported once as a critical error.
* v2/plugin: Loader registers plugins with the repeatable -plugin flag
  (resolved through Bazel runfiles, the current directory, the
  workspace directory, or PATH) or with "# gazelle:plugin path [args]"
  in the repository root build file. update.Run starts plugins after
  flags are parsed and adds them to the set of extensions, so the
  default gazelle binary and custom gazelle_binary targets both
  support them.
* v2/plugin/server: helper for writing plugins in Go.
* v2/plugin/examples/sh: reference plugin for shell scripts, in Python
  (standard library only) and in Go. Tests run Gazelle end to end with
  both and check that they produce the same build files.

Fixes #938
